# aqualog2nc: Convert data in Origin Pro-type OPJ files containing Horiba AquaLog EEM+Absorbance to NetCDF files.
-----------------------------


## USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:
-----------------------------

1. macOS (Apple Silicon only):
	- Download aqualog2nc-macos-arm64
	- Double click on aqualog2nc-macos-arm64 (do not move to trash when promted)
	- Go to Settings -> Security & Privacy -> scroll down -> approve the application
	- Open terminal -> change to directory containing aqualog2nc-macos-arm64 -> run "chmod +x aqualog2nc-macos-arm64"  (making the software exectutable)
	- Usage: ./aqualog2nc-macos-arm64 <input.opj | input_folder> output.nc (e.g. ./aqualog2nc-macos-arm64 /Users/wuensch/test.opj test.nc)
	- NetCDF file will appear in the current directory of the terminal (not the directory with the OPJ files)

2. Windows
	- Download aqualog2nc-windows-x64.exe
	- Open the executable -> On the blue pop-up, click "more info" -> Run anyway
	- Open Terminal -> change to directory containing aqualog2nc-windows-x64.exe
	- Usage: ./aqualog2nc-windows-x64 <input.opj | input_folder> output.nc (e.g. ./aqualog2nc-windows-x64 "C:\Users\Public\Documents\Jobin Yvon\" test.nc)
	- NetCDF file will appear in the current directory of the terminal (not the directory with the OPJ files)

3. Linux
	I don't have a machine running Linux, so I could not produce a walk-through. Expect it to be similar to macOS.

## ATTRIBUTION
-----------------------------

aqualog2nc is derived from the liborigin project:

https://github.com/gerlachs/liborigin

liborigin is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 (GPL-3.0).

aqualog2nc extends liborigin with support for extracting Horiba AquaLog
EEM and absorbance data and exporting the results to NetCDF.

Original liborigin authors include Stefan Gerlach and contributors.
